\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  VSJoin integrated execution pipeline. Data plane (top) combines four mechanisms: micro-batch admission (M4), coarse routing with load signals (M2), pointer multicast to selected workers (M4), worker-local fine-centroid indexing (M1), exact verification, and emission. Control plane (bottom) runs asynchronously: load monitor tracks centroid-level load, split controller detects hot regions, and versioned routing table coordinates atomic publication without hot-path locking.\relax }}{7}{figure.caption.36}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:vsjoin-architecture}{{1}{7}{VSJoin integrated execution pipeline. Data plane (top) combines four mechanisms: micro-batch admission (M4), coarse routing with load signals (M2), pointer multicast to selected workers (M4), worker-local fine-centroid indexing (M1), exact verification, and emission. Control plane (bottom) runs asynchronously: load monitor tracks centroid-level load, split controller detects hot regions, and versioned routing table coordinates atomic publication without hot-path locking.\relax }{figure.caption.36}{}}
